{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 7.681,
   "text": "Every payphone on Route 9 has the same faded sticker."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 8.281,
   "end": 12.42,
   "text": "It says: if this phone rings... it's for you. Do not answer."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 13.32,
   "end": 17.779,
   "text": "My little sister and I were driving all night to our dad's place."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 18.379,
   "end": 22.944,
   "text": "Around three a.m., I pulled over. She stayed asleep in the car."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 23.644,
   "end": 28.743,
   "text": "The lot was empty. Just me, a humming vending machine... and that payphone."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 29.543,
   "end": 30.78,
   "text": "Then it rang."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 33.78,
   "end": 37.087,
   "text": "I didn't move. Twelve rings... then silence."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 37.887,
   "end": 41.769,
   "text": "My cell buzzed. The caller ID was the payphone."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 42.569,
   "end": 46.943,
   "text": "I let it ring out. One voicemail. No words. Just breathing."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 47.843,
   "end": 52.109,
   "text": "Then, behind me, my sister's phone lit up inside the car."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 53.909,
   "end": 58.197,
   "text": "I watched her answer it, half asleep. She nodded... and hung up."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 59.097,
   "end": 61.999,
   "text": "I tapped on the glass. Who was that?"
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 62.999,
   "end": 68.737,
   "text": "She stared right at me. It was you. You said to lock the doors... and not to let you back in."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 69.737,
   "end": 71.657,
   "text": "The locks clicked shut."
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "start": 72.857,
   "end": 79.727,
   "text": "And behind me, the payphone's receiver swung on its cord... and my own voice whispered, Good. Don't let him in."
  }
 ],
